<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26403" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐδακ-τός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Erx.</u>
			398d
		</span></i>: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of things, <i>taught,
				learnt,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅπαντα γάρ σοι τἀμὰ νουθετήματα κείνης
				διδακτά</span>
			<i>of</i> her <i>teaching,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				344
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἀνθρωπίνης σοφίας λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>1 Ep.Cor.</u>
					2.13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσοις δ. μηδέν, ἀλλ᾽ ἐν τῇ φύσει τὸ
					σωφρονεῖν εἴληχεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hipp.</u>
					79
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that can be taught</i> or <i>learnt,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δ.</span>”
				<i>things which may be taught by study and experience,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					3.41
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρρητα,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				300
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίδαξον . . εἰ διδακτά
			μοι</span> if I <i>may learn</i> them, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				64
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				671
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ μὲν δ. μανθάνω, τὰ δ᾽ εὑρετὰ ζητῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					843
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κἄστ᾽ οὐ διδακτόν</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ τῆς τύχης</span>) <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				786
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				914
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καθ᾽ ὅσον δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					13.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετὴν . . εἴτε δ. εἴ τε μὴ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Men.</u>
					71a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Prt.</u>
				328c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Euthd.</u>
				274e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιστήμη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1139b25
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>taught, instructed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πολέμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>1 Ma.</u>
					4.7
				</span></i>
			; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. θεοῦ</span>
			<i>taught</i> by God, ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Is.</u>
				54.13
			</span></i>( =
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Jo.</u>
				6.45
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
